Created by: S. M. Riordan & W. R. J. Tomlinson

This is a two-player platformer game for the UCFK4 using a scrolling LED matrix display,
synchronised player readiness and win/loss detection via IR communication.
    - The game is to played horizontally with the right side being UCFK4 TOP and left side UCFK4 BOTTOM.
    - The map scrolls continuously from right to left, creating platforms at different heights.
    - Each player controls a single pixel representing their character.
    - If a player falls to the bottom row with no platform beneath them, they lose.
    - If a player collides with the side of an approaching platform, they lose.
    - The game gets faster each time the map loops.

Controls:
    Action:     Navswitch Direction:
    Jump        North
    Fall        South

To initialise "Ready-Up" sequence with between players:
    - Press "SW3" to display "LED1" ready indicator,
    - Once both players are ready, the game starts!

Once the game is over, the players will be returned to the "Ready-Up" screen.


Statement of AI use:

Portions of this project, including code structuring, function documentation, and gameplay description text, 
were drafted with assistance from OpenAI’s ChatGPT. 
All AI-generated content was reviewed, modified, and validated manually to ensure correctness and suitability 
for this specific embedded platform.